1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,362
Admin Templates lets you change how parts of the Orchard Core admin are

2
00:00:05,362 --> 00:00:09,385
drawn, using Liquid templates that you write in the admin itself.

3
00:00:09,385 --> 00:00:13,691
In this video, we enable the feature, replace the Visit Site link, and

4
00:00:13,691 --> 00:00:16,240
see how templates travel with a recipe.

5
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,849
The admin is drawn by shapes.

6
00:00:22,849 --> 00:00:27,212
To change one, you normally override its view in a custom admin theme,

7
00:00:27,212 --> 00:00:30,370
which means changing code and deploying the site.

8
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:34,795
The Admin Templates feature moves that change into the admin.

9
00:00:34,795 --> 00:00:38,854
You write a Liquid template, name it after a shape, and Orchard Core

10
00:00:38,854 --> 00:00:42,090
stores it in the database and uses it on admin pages.

11
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:47,193
Admin Templates apply only to the admin, and the Templates feature does the

12
00:00:47,193 --> 00:00:48,751
same for the front end.

13
00:00:48,751 --> 00:00:52,459
A template wins over a view file of the same name, and deleting

14
00:00:52,459 --> 00:00:54,340
it brings the view file back.

15
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,847
A template is named after a shape.

16
00:01:00,847 --> 00:01:05,404
The name is the shape type or an alternate, where double underscores take

17
00:01:05,404 --> 00:01:08,173
the place of the dash in a view file name.

18
00:01:08,173 --> 00:01:10,250
In Liquid, the shape is Model.

19
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,872
The documentation overrides these admin shapes with Admin Templates.

20
00:01:15,872 --> 00:01:22,324
AdminBranding draws the logo and site name, VisitSiteNavbarItem the Visit Site link, Message

21
00:01:22,324 --> 00:01:27,460
one notification, and NotifyMessages the container of the notifications.

22
00:01:31,693 --> 00:01:36,954
Admin Templates is a feature of the Templates module, so it has to be enabled first.

23
00:01:36,954 --> 00:01:40,403
Open Tools, Features, and search for admin templates.

24
00:01:40,859 --> 00:01:45,642
The feature is listed under Development, with Templates as its dependency.

25
00:01:45,642 --> 00:01:46,837
Select Enable.

26
00:01:46,837 --> 00:01:51,799
A notification confirms it, and any feature it depends on is enabled with it.

27
00:01:52,253 --> 00:01:56,143
The Design menu has an Admin Templates entry beside Templates.

28
00:01:56,143 --> 00:01:56,944
Open it.

29
00:01:56,944 --> 00:02:01,063
The list is empty, and says there are no templates for the moment.

30
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:06,746
Select Add Template.

31
00:02:06,746 --> 00:02:10,348
The form asks for a Name, a Description, and the Content.

32
00:02:10,348 --> 00:02:14,520
Unlike the form of the Templates feature, it has no Preview button.

33
00:02:14,974 --> 00:02:16,867
The name is the shape type.

34
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:21,513
Enter VisitSiteNavbarItem, the shape of the Visit Site link in the top bar,

35
00:02:21,513 --> 00:02:23,234
and a short description.

36
00:02:23,688 --> 00:02:25,940
Content is an editor for Liquid.

37
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,600
We enter the template:

38
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:32,638
the absolute URL filter builds the link, and the t filter translates the label.

39
00:02:33,107 --> 00:02:37,246
It draws the same link as the original, with the words Visit Site

40
00:02:37,246 --> 00:02:38,878
added beside the icon.

41
00:02:38,878 --> 00:02:44,007
A template replaces the whole shape, so it has to draw everything the shape shows.

42
00:02:44,476 --> 00:02:45,455
Select Save.

43
00:02:45,455 --> 00:02:50,023
A notification confirms that the template has been created, and the list shows

44
00:02:50,023 --> 00:02:53,666
it with its description, an Edit button, and a Delete button.

45
00:02:54,124 --> 00:02:55,606
Look at the top bar:

46
00:02:55,606 --> 00:02:58,685
the Visit Site link shows its icon and its text.

47
00:02:58,685 --> 00:03:03,074
The template applies to every page of the admin, such as Content Items.

48
00:03:07,291 --> 00:03:10,941
Edit opens the same form with the saved name and Liquid.

49
00:03:10,941 --> 00:03:14,180
Change the text beside the icon, and select Save.

50
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:16,241
The top bar shows the change.

51
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,956
Delete asks for confirmation.

52
00:03:18,956 --> 00:03:23,281
Confirm it, and a notification says the template was deleted.

53
00:03:23,281 --> 00:03:25,217
The list is empty again.

54
00:03:25,671 --> 00:03:31,141
The original view was never touched, so the top bar shows the icon alone again.

55
00:03:35,341 --> 00:03:39,141
A recipe creates admin templates with the AdminTemplates step.

56
00:03:39,141 --> 00:03:43,836
Each property is a template name, holding its Description and its Content, and

57
00:03:43,836 --> 00:03:46,741
the content can point to a file of the recipe.

58
00:03:47,491 --> 00:03:52,723
In a deployment plan, the All Admin Templates step exports every admin template.

59
00:03:52,723 --> 00:03:57,286
With Export templates as files, each one is written to a Liquid file,

60
00:03:57,286 --> 00:04:00,571
and the plan's AdminTemplates step points to it.

61
00:04:04,771 --> 00:04:08,471
Save checks that the name and the content are filled in, and that

62
00:04:08,471 --> 00:04:10,659
no other template has the same name.

63
00:04:10,659 --> 00:04:14,671
If the Liquid cannot be parsed, the shape shows the parser's error text

64
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:17,901
instead of your markup, so test each template on a page.

65
00:04:18,651 --> 00:04:20,296
Two permissions apply:

66
00:04:20,296 --> 00:04:26,346
Manage admin templates, granted to Administrator by default, and Manage Liquid templates, granted

67
00:04:26,346 --> 00:04:28,342
to Administrator and Editor.

68
00:04:28,342 --> 00:04:31,631
Both are security critical, and a user needs both.

69
00:04:32,381 --> 00:04:35,883
A multi-tenant host can keep the feature away from a tenant.

70
00:04:35,883 --> 00:04:40,340
A feature profile with an Exclude rule for the Admin Templates feature removes

71
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:44,001
it from the features available to tenants that use the profile.

72
00:04:46,001 --> 00:04:49,783
Admin Templates keeps changes to the admin inside the admin:

73
00:04:49,783 --> 00:04:55,742
Liquid templates named after shapes, stored in the database, and moved between sites with recipes.

74
00:04:55,742 --> 00:04:57,231
Thanks for watching.

